<listPerson>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-ii"><persName>Heinrich II.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Includes Burggraf Heinrich II. von Plauen (1429-1446), Heinrich II. von Gera (1602-1670), Heinrich II. von Burgk (two persons), Heinrich II. von Köstritz (1803-1852), Heinrich II. von Lobenstein (d. 1782) and Heinrich II. von Obergreiz (1696-1722).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-iii"><persName>Heinrich III.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Includes Burggraf Heinrich III. von Plauen (1446-1482), Heinrich III. von Schleiz (1603-1640), Heinrich III. von Lobenstein (1648-1710), Heinrich III. von Untergreiz (1701-1768) and Heinrich III. von Burgk (d. 1640).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-li-fuerst-reuss-ebersdorf"><persName>Heinrich LI. (Fürst Reuß-Ebersdorf)</persName><note>Heinrich LI., „der Gute", Graf, seit 1806 Fürst Reuß zu Ebersdorf; geb. 1761, regierte 1779-1822, 1802 Mitregent in Gera und Saalburg; verheiratet mit Louise von Hoym; Vater Heinrichs LXXII. und Schwiegervater Heinrichs LXVII.; bewirtete 1806 Napoleon in Ebersdorf.</note><idno type="Wikidata">https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q642401</idno></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-liv-fuerst-reuss-lobenstein-selbitz"><persName>Heinrich LIV. (Fürst Reuß-Lobenstein-Selbitz)</persName><note>Heinrich LIV., Neffe Heinrichs XXI. aus der Nebenlinie Selbitz; geb. 1767, erbte 1805 Lobenstein, 1806 Reichsfürst, † 1824 ohne Nachkommen (Lobenstein fiel an Ebersdorf); verheiratet 1) Marie von Stolberg-Wernigerode, 2) Franziska Reuß-Köstritz.</note><idno type="Wikidata">https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q55875295</idno></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-lxxii-fuerst-reuss-lobenstein-ebersdorf"><persName>Heinrich LXXII. (Fürst Reuß-Lobenstein-Ebersdorf)</persName><note>Heinrich LXXII., Fürst von Lobenstein-Ebersdorf, einziger Sohn Heinrichs LI.; geb. 1797, regierte 1822-1848 (Verzicht am 1. Okt. 1848), † Febr. 1853 in Dresden als letzter männlicher Sproß des Specialhauses Lobenstein; nannte die alte Landesvertretung „verrottet".</note><idno type="Wikidata">https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q215069</idno></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-viii"><persName>Heinrich VIII.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Includes Heinrich VIII. Herr von Hirschberg (1652-1711) and several short-lived princes in the tables.</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-x"><persName>Heinrich X.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Includes Heinrich X. von Lobenstein (1621-1671; see the separate entry "Heinrich X. v. Lobenstein"), Heinrich X. von Ebersdorf (1662-1711) and Prince Heinrich X. (1827-1847, Köstritz).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-xv"><persName>Heinrich XV.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Includes Heinrich XV. von Lobenstein (1674-1739), Heinrich XV. von Obergreiz (1676-1690), Heinrich XV. von Greiz (1751-1825, Imperial general), Prince Heinrich XV. (b. 1834).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-xxiv"><persName>Heinrich XXIV.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Heinrich XXIV. von Köstritz (1681-1748), Heinrich XXIV. von Ebersdorf (1724-1779) and a prince born 1855 (Köstritz).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-xxix"><persName>Heinrich XXIX.</persName><note>ambiguous; refers to different persons. The numeral is counted afresh in every century and separately for the elder and younger line of Reuss (Brückner p. 376), so the same form denotes different princes; see the genealogical tables pp. 341-402. Mostly Heinrich XXIX. von Ebersdorf (1699-1747), but also a prince born 1860 (Köstritz).</note></person>
<person xml:id="person-heinrich-xxxv-fuerst-reuss-lobenstein"><persName>Heinrich XXXV. (Fürst Reuß-Lobenstein)</persName><note>Heinrich XXXV., Graf, seit 1790 Reichsfürst von Reuß-Lobenstein; geb. 1738, 1802 Mitregent von Gera, † 1805 ohne Erben (Lobenstein fiel an Heinrich LIV.).</note><idno type="Wikidata">https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q119076424</idno></person>
</listPerson>
